 "reading": "20129: a request with no header gets stacked [session-dedup, ccr, lite] (source default); `off` gives no engine (source request-header). The header `allow-lossy` does not select the ten-engine operator plan of the engines map: a stored combo named allow-lossy exists on 20129 (a peer-owned row; eleven engines including headroom), and a named combo is matched before the keyword is consulted (planResolution.ts:56-57 at 2f42a9ac1), so it resolves to that combo with source request-header. The seeded 'Standard Savings' combo is [session-dedup, lite]. 20128 as running (master off, codex/* excluded): every header gives off. With the master on and the exclusion removed, a headerless request would still resolve to off (its engines map is not explicit and defaultMode is off), while `engine:lite` and the Standard Savings combo would resolve to their engines: enabling the headerless lane there needs the engines map stored as well as the master switch."
}
